-- 199_ranked_match_settings.surql -- MvC2 Steam RANKED match settings: the per-game settings descriptor
-- table, the three config fillers (ranked column / casual column / local defaults), the matchmaking
-- chooser, the wire blob, read timing, the ranked session shape, online-only game-code branches and the
-- SUPERGUN RANKED preset write-set. 2026-09-06. RE METHOD: seed on unique constants (table columns,
-- 0x2c2c stride, string id 0x3f9, DAT_140a69de0 groups), propagate along the call graph, translate
-- through the block map (G = blk+0x3CB8 <-> 0x8c268240), tag CONFIRMED/INFERRED, store edges.
-- Forward slashes only in ref/note; no apostrophes.
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:ranked_settings_re_20260906 SET kind='disasm', strength='code',
  ref='Ghidra dumpproj / mvc_dump.bin: FUN_14003c130, FUN_140050ec0, FUN_140050d90, FUN_140050cf0, FUN_14004aba0, FUN_14004aa10, FUN_14004aa60, FUN_14004a9c0, FUN_14004add0, FUN_14003fd50, FUN_140040140, FUN_140049b50, FUN_140050830, FUN_140050470, FUN_140037370, FUN_140037b50, FUN_140608690, FUN_140607b50, FUN_1400925d0, FUN_140096af0, FUN_14003bad0, FUN_140094590, FUN_140093640, FUN_140093c60, FUN_1400accd0, FUN_140098480, FUN_140098c20, FUN_140098d40, FUN_140098670, FUN_1400993b0, FUN_14008dbd0, FUN_14008e620, FUN_14007e5d0, FUN_1400676c0 (0x140067f02 case), FUN_140068670, FUN_14003fa60, FUN_140628df0, FUN_140619910, FUN_140619b00, FUN_140619970, FUN_14063a4a0, FUN_14063abb0, FUN_14063cd30, FUN_14068ff30, 0x140707660 (no Ghidra fn, capstone), FUN_140608bf0, FUN_140616050, FUN_14062e110, FUN_14062e090, caseD_0 0x14060bf81; tables 0x140a4e030 (game records, stride 0x50), 0x140a35068 (settings descriptors, stride 0x2c2c, entries 0x24), 0x140a4859c (mvsc2 table), DAT_140a69de0, DAT_140a97e3c, DAT_140a6fa74, DAT_140a31020, DAT_14097eb40 = 0.03125; register-keyed reader scans of config/G/blk/session offsets over the whole image; SH4 refs/marvelous2/work.asm lines 20-21 (0x8C268270 Char Unlocks, 0x8c268278 Color Unlocks).',
  note='Scratchpad ranked_settings.md (session 193726f3). All Steam addresses are live addresses (no ASLR).';

UPSERT source:ranked_anchor_readings_20260906 SET kind='capture', strength='reproduction',
  ref='mvc-live-skins-quarters/d3dcap/ttd/runs/vs-01/pre, select-01/pre, 20260903-000941/pre: exe_image.bin config+0x284..0x2c8 and mode words, host_device.bin session words, blk.bin G bytes.',
  note='config+0x28c..0x2b0 = [2,1,1,2,2,0,0,7,1,1] and G+0x28 = 0 in all three; vs-01 config+0x80c = 1, 0x7b4/0x7b8/0x7bc = 0, 0x7f4 = 0, session 0xd0338 = 1, 0xd0320/0xd0328/0xd0374/0xd037c = 0, hostdev+0x1cd = 0, +0x1b8 = 0.';

UPSERT finding:mvc2_match_settings_descriptor_table SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-06',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='The Fighting Collection game settings are a static per-game descriptor table: 0x140a35068 + idx*0x2c2c, 9 ints per setting, columns default / CASUAL / RANKED; MvC2 (gameId 5, idx 7) has 10 settings mapped to config+0x28c + 4*i',
  statement='Game record table 0x140a4e030 + gameId*0x50 (7 games, rom names at rec+8/+0x10; mvsc2 = gameId 5 @0x140a4e1c0); rec+0x3b (DAT_140a4e06b) = descriptor index (mvsc2 -> 7), rec+0x3c (DAT_140a4e06c, FUN_14004a800) = players 2, rec+0x44/0x46/0x48 u16 -> config+0x284/0x286/0x288 (FUN_140049b50; mvsc2 0xff x3, no MvC2 reader). Descriptor table 0x140a35068 + idx*0x2c2c: int count then entries at +4 + i*0x24: +0 kind (FUN_14004ad30), +4 choices (FUN_14004ace0), +8 default (FUN_14004a9c0), +0xc casual column (FUN_14004aa10), +0x10 RANKED column (FUN_14004aa60), +0x14 (FUN_14004ad80), +0x18 string id (FUN_14004aab0), +0x1c (FUN_14004ab00), +0x20 (FUN_14004ab50). MvC2 table @0x140a4859c count 10, rows [kind,choices,default,casual,ranked,strid]: 0 [0,9,2,2,2,0x3ab] config+0x28c difficulty (FUN_140607b50: config+0x4dc = v-1 -> G+0x4f -> G+0x83 CPU level); 1 [0,4,1,1,1,0x3ad] config+0x290 damage -> G+0x1b -> DAT_140a97e3c = 0x10/0x20/0x30/0x40 x(1/32) in FUN_14063cd30 = x0.5/1.0/1.5/2.0; 2 [0,4,1,1,1,0x3b3] config+0x294 timer speed -> G+0x46 -> DAT_140a6fa74 = 180/120/90/70 frames per clock tick; 3 [0,7,5,5,2,0x3be] config+0x298 game speed -> G+0x49 (seed 189: 2 = TURBO1 period 4, 5 = free select); 4 [1,3,2,2,2,0x30d] config+0x29c coin mode -> blk+0x3c40 = (v==2) FREE PLAY, blk+0x3c43 = (v==1)+1, forced 2 when config+0x828 or +0x7c0; 5 [1,2,0,0,0,0x309] config+0x2a0 arcade attract gate (caseD_0 0x14060bf81, skipped in training/versus/spectate); 6 [1,2,0,1,1,0x3f9] config+0x2a4 -> G+0x28 screen flash suppression (see finding:screen_flash_setting_G_0x28); 7 [1,8,7,7,7,0x400] config+0x2a8 secret character unlock groups -> FUN_140608690 loops DAT_140a69de0 (7 groups x 4 char ids) into G+0x30/G+0x34 (SH4 0x8C268270 Char Unlocks); 8 [1,3,1,1,1,0x419] config+0x2ac extra colours: v != 0 -> G+0x38/0x3c = G+0x30/0x34 (SH4 0x8c268278 Color Unlocks), v == 2 -> blk+0x33a15 = 1 (FUN_140628df0); 9 [1,2,0,1,1,0xa62] config+0x2b0 -> keeps entity+0x2b5 attack multiplier across the per-character reset 0x140707660 (see finding:setting9_config_0x2b0_attack_multiplier_keep). Settings 10..15 do not exist for MvC2, so config+0x2b4..0x2c8 are never written by the fillers (0 in every anchor).',
  consequence='The RANKED rule set for MvC2 is the literal column [2,1,1,2,2,0,1,7,1,1] at 0x140a485a0 + i*0x24 + 0x10. The CASUAL column is identical except setting 3 (speed 5 = free select). Names difficulty / timer speed / coin mode / secret characters / extra colours are INFERRED from readers; the string ids 0x3ab.. live in the localisation files, not the exe. Damage and speed mechanics are CONFIRMED from code.';

UPSERT finding:ranked_settings_are_a_static_column SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-06',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='RANKED settings are never negotiated: FUN_14003c130 (match found) calls FUN_140050ec0 iff session+0xd0374 == 1, which copies the RANKED column into config+0x28c..; casual uses FUN_140050d90 (casual column); offline uses FUN_140050cf0 (persisted or default)',
  statement='FUN_140050ec0(hostdev): for i < count, config+0x28c+4i = RANKED column (+0x10) or FUN_14004aba0 local default when the column is negative. FUN_140050d90(hostdev, flag): CASUAL column (+0xc); flag = 1 makes string-id-0x3f9 settings take the local default (used by the custom lobby quick create FUN_1400accd0 state 2 and the options viewer mode 5). FUN_140050cf0(hostdev): FUN_14004aba0 = persisted save value save+0x1f0 + (game*0x26b + i)*4 (FUN_14003fd50; initialised from the default column by FUN_140040140) if < choices, else the table default. FUN_14003c130: hostdev+0x1ac = session+0xd03e4 (game), +0x1b0 = 0xd03e8 (variant), 0xd0330 = 0, 0xd0338 = 0, FUN_140050830 (config+8 game, +0xc variant, rom ptrs), FUN_140049b50 (config+0x284..0x288), then IF session+0xd0374 == 1 THEN FUN_140050ec0 ELSE FUN_140050d90(0); config+0x7f4 = 2; FUN_140051150 (key config config+0x2dc); FUN_140050470(1) -> hostdev+0x1cd = 1; session+0xd037c = 1; scene switch to PTR_PTR_140ab6780. Menu chain: FUN_1400925d0 case 7 (online top menu) writes session+0xd0320 = item (1 = matchmaking/versus family, 0/2/3/4 other modes); FUN_140096af0 case 4 writes 0xd0328 = menu index and, from the item value, 0xd0374 = 0 (state 5, casual search) / 1 (state 6, RANKED search) / 2 (state 7, custom lobby, 0xd03ec = 0); FUN_14003bad0 (join by link) writes 0xd0320 = 1, 0xd0374 = 2, 0xd0328 = 2; the search object FUN_140094590 writes 0xd037c = 3 while searching. FUN_14004aa60 (ranked column accessor) has exactly one caller, the options VIEWER FUN_140098d40 mode 4; the live path reads the column inline in FUN_140050ec0.',
  consequence='Both ranked peers derive identical config+0x28c.. from the same image bytes; nothing about the ranked rule set travels over the wire or depends on either player. Ranked vs casual differs ONLY in setting 3 (speed 2 vs 5); session+0xd0374 and its mirror config+0x7b8 have NO reader in game code.';

UPSERT finding:lobby_match_settings_blob_layout SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-06',
  title='The lobby match-settings blob is netmgr+0x2548 (DAT_140bd3bb8+0x2548): +8 game, +9 variant, +0xa players, +0xb+i setting i -> config+0x28c+4i; edited by the room options object FUN_140098480 and applied by FUN_14008e620',
  statement='blob = *(lobbyScene+0x350) = lobbyOptionsObj+0x340 = DAT_140bd3bb8 + 0x2548 (FUN_140098480 stores DAT_140bd3bb8+0x2548 at obj+0x340; FUN_14007e5d0 writes it directly: +0x2548 u16 = 1, +0x2550 game = hostdev+0x1ac, +0x2551 variant, +0x2552 = FUN_14004a800 players, +0x2553.. = config+0x28c.. bytes). Receivers: FUN_1400676c0 case @0x140067f02 copies msg+4..+0x1f into blob and blob+0xb.. into config+0x28c.. (local default substituted where the casual column is negative); FUN_140068670 type 2: msg+8 game, +9 variant, msg+0xa+i -> config+0x28c+4i, msg+0x1a/0x1b/0x1c -> config+0x284/0x286/0x288 u16, msg+0x1d -> config+0x7f4; lobby scene FUN_14008dbd0 state 10 = FUN_14008e620: options object obj+0x384[i] (count obj+0x348, game obj+0x3c4, variant obj+0x3c8) -> blob+0xb+i -> config+0x28c+4i (host only, FUN_1400669e0 != 0), then hostdev+0x1ac/+0x1b0 = blob+8/+9. Options object modes (FUN_140098480 4th arg): 1 host edit, 2 view, 3 casual-column view, 4 RANKED-column view, 5 quick create, 6 punisher co-op; FUN_140098d40 fills obj+0x384/+0x3d4/+0x424/+0x474/+0x4c4/+0x514.. from the descriptor columns (mode 3 casual, 4 ranked, 5 casual-with-0x3f9-local, 6 or param_2 from blob+0xb+i). The persisted settings blob is a different thing: FUN_14003fa60 reads save+0x5a2f5.. (3 u16 then 16 bytes) into config+0x284..0x2c8.',
  consequence='For SUPERGUN nothing in the blob matters: the runner writes config directly. The blob layout is recorded so a future lobby/netcode layer can read or emit it without re-deriving; the 128-byte Steam BinaryData blob is a different object (lobby-info +0x50) and remains UNKNOWN.';

UPSERT finding:settings_read_timing_mode_entry_vs_round SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-06',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='config settings are baked into G ONCE per mode entry by FUN_140608690 (arena carve FUN_140607b50); the sim then reads the G bytes per event, so a config write takes effect at the next mode entry and a G write at the next reader event',
  statement='FUN_140607b50 (per mode entry): config+0x4dc = config[0x28c] - 1 (or 0x4e4 = 1 if < 1), then FUN_140608690: G+0x4f = config[0x4dc], G+0x1b = config[0x290], G+0x46 = config[0x294], G+0x49 = config[0x298], G+0x28 = config[0x2a4], G+0x4d = 2, G+0x30/0x34 from config[0x2a8] groups, G+0x38/0x3c = G+0x30/0x34 iff config[0x2ac] != 0, blk+0x3c40/0x3c43 from config[0x29c] (forced 2 when config+0x828 or +0x7c0). Scene entry caseD_3 then sets G+0x4d = 3 iff config+0x828 and G+0x2a = 1 iff config+0x7c0. Per-event readers: G+0x1b every hit (FUN_14063cd30 damage formula); G+0x46 and G+0x4d every clock tick (FUN_140626fe0), G+0x4d at round init (FUN_1406274f0); G+0x49 at the select confirm (G+0x89, 0x14062a0fc) and the round block (FUN_140628020); G+0x28 at every flash request (FUN_140619910 / FUN_140619b00); G+0x30..0x3c plus config+0x2ac at select entry per side (FUN_140628df0); config+0x2b0 at the per-character reset method 0x140707660; config+0x28c only in FUN_140607b50.',
  consequence='Runner rule: write the config page BEFORE FUN_140608690 runs (before any mode entry or re-carve); if blk is restored after the carve, write the G bytes directly. A mid-round G write is legal but only lands at the next event of that reader.';

UPSERT finding:ranked_session_config_shape SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-06',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='What an online RANKED match looks like in session / config / G, and how it differs from the vs-01 local-versus anchor: exactly two settings (config+0x2a4 -> G+0x28, config+0x2b0) plus mode words',
  statement='session (hostdev): 0xd0374 = 1 (CONFIRMED test in FUN_14003c130), 0xd037c = 1 (CONFIRMED write in FUN_14003c130), 0xd0330 = 0, 0xd0338 = 0 (CONFIRMED), hostdev+0x1cd = 1 (FUN_140050470(1)), +0x1ac = 5, +0x1b0 = variant, 0xd0320 = 1 and 0xd0328 = 1 (INFERRED: menu path FUN_1400925d0 item 1 / FUN_140096af0 index 1, and live traces in memory notes). config via FUN_140037370 / FUN_140037b50: 0x7b4 = 1 (0xd0320 == 1, 0xd0328 != 4, 0xd037c == 1), 0x7b8 = 1 (= 0xd0374), 0x7bc = 1 (= hostdev+0x1cd), 0x7c8 = 0, 0x7f8 = 0, 0x828 = 0, 0x82c = 0, 0x80c = 0, 0x4e0 = 1, 0x794 = 1, 0x7c0 = 1, 0x7c4 = 0xd03ec, 0x7f4 = 2, 0x7d8 = 0xd03f4. G after FUN_140608690 + caseD_3: G+0x2a = 1, G+0x4d = 2, G+0xa6 = 0, G+0x4c = 0, G+0x49 = 2, G+0x1b = 1, G+0x46 = 1, G+0x28 = 1, G+0x4f = 1, G+0x30/0x34 = G+0x38/0x3c = 0xf8ffffff/0x07ffffff, blk+0x3c40 = 1, blk+0x3c43 = 1. Anchor readings (vs-01, select-01, 20260903-000941): config+0x28c..0x2b0 = [2,1,1,2,2,0,0,7,1,1], G+0x28 = 0; vs-01 has config+0x80c = 1, 0x7b4/0x7b8/0x7bc = 0, 0x7f4 = 0, session 0xd0338 = 1, all other mode words 0, hostdev+0x1cd = 0, +0x1b8 = 0.',
  consequence='Relative to vs-01 the RANKED rule set differs in config+0x2a4 (0 -> 1, G+0x28 0 -> 1: KO/hit screen flash off) and config+0x2b0 (0 -> 1: attack multiplier kept across the per-character reset). Speed, damage, timer, unlocks and colours are already the ranked values in every anchor because the user persisted speed 2. The mode words (0x7b4/0x7b8/0x7bc/0x80c, session words) only matter through the branches in finding:online_only_game_code_branches.';

UPSERT finding:online_only_game_code_branches SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-06',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='Inside MvC2 game code the online flags are read at exactly four sites: config+0x7b4 gates the select-entry blk snapshot/restore FUN_140608bf0; config+0x7bc gates the high-score insert FUN_140616050 and the name-entry timeout FUN_14062e110; session+0xd0374 / config+0x7b8 (ranked) are never read',
  statement='Register-keyed scan of every load of 0x140acd3a0 / 0x140acd3a8 followed by a displacement on the loaded register, restricted to 0x140600000..0x140900000: config+0x7b4 readers 0x140608bfb / 0x140608d4f (FUN_140608bf0, called only from FUN_140611A20 caseD_2 = every select-phase entry: when 0x7b4 == 0 && 0x828 == 0 it copies blk into *(0x142edf568)+8 on the first entry (568[0] = 1, 568[1] = G+0x18, config+0x528 = 1; 0x7c8 != 0 -> 0x7cc = 1) and on later entries copies it back and re-points blk+0x32500..0x32528 to the six fighter structs); config+0x7bc readers 0x14061605c (FUN_140616050, FUN_14060E170 caseD_8: high-score table blk+0x327d8 insertion, skipped when 0x7bc || 0x828 || 0x7f8 || 0x4e8) and 0x14062e159 (FUN_14062e110: forces the name-entry countdown fighter+0x64c to expire; inside FUN_14062e090 which returns immediately when G+0x2a != 0 or G+0x4c == 2, so dead in versus); config+0x7c8 readers 0x140608c71 / 0x140608db4 (inside FUN_140608bf0); config+0x7f8 readers 0x14060bf77, 0x140615d0a, 0x140616076, 0x1406324f7/0x140632500 (spectator). session+0xd0374 and config+0x7b8 have zero readers above 0x1400b0000. The 540-frame 1P WIN park (seed 184, FUN_140614CC0) is gated by config+0x7c0 (versus), identical in ranked; stage select and the select timer have no online reader.',
  consequence='Reproducing a ranked match offline needs no online flag for the sim itself: the only sim-visible consequence of config+0x7b4 = 1 is that the select-entry snapshot/restore does not run (relevant to rematch flows that return to select), and of config+0x7bc = 1 that no high-score entry is written after a match. Ranked adds nothing beyond the settings column.';

UPSERT finding:screen_flash_setting_G_0x28 SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-06',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='config+0x2a4 -> G+0x28 (blk+0x3CE0) is the screen-flash suppression byte: the white strobe requests FUN_140619910 / FUN_140619b00 only write the flash record blk+0x6ce8/0x6cec/0x6cf0 when G+0x28 == 0; online forces 1 (flash off), offline default 0 (flash on)',
  statement='FUN_140619910: if G+0x28 == 0 { blk+0x6ce8 = 1 (type), +0x6cec = 0x10 (frames), +0x6cf0 = 0xffffff (white) }; callers FUN_14073d490 and caseD_4 0x14079fd62. FUN_140619b00: if G+0x28 == 0 { type 6, 0x18 frames, white }; callers FUN_14063a4a0 (KO branch: fighter+0x578 == 0 && +0x28c == 0 -> +0x28c = 0xff, hitstop 10, flash), FUN_14063abb0, FUN_14063cbc0, FUN_14063ac80. FUN_140619970 consumes the record every frame: types 1/3/4/5/6 -> blk+0x6ce4 = (frames >> 1) & 1 (strobe every 2 frames), type 2 -> frames & 1, 7/8 -> 2, 9 -> 3, decrementing +0x6cec; other writers use types 8/9 with colour 0 (fade to black). Descriptor row 6 (strid 0x3f9, 2 choices, default 0, casual 1, ranked 1) is the one row the custom-lobby quick create and the viewer mode 5 take from the LOCAL setting instead of the column (FUN_140050d90 flag, FUN_140098d40 mode 5). No G+0x28 writer exists on the SH4 side (0x8c268268 is unannotated in refs/marvelous2), so the byte is a collection-era addition to GameGlobal.',
  caveat='The option NAME is INFERRED from the mechanism (a flashing-effects / photosensitivity toggle); the exe carries no label. Polarity is CONFIRMED from the set-site: 0 = flashes drawn, 1 = suppressed.',
  consequence='A ranked-faithful runner sets G+0x28 = 1 (no white KO strobe in blk+0x6ce4). This is a visible render difference against every existing anchor (G+0x28 = 0) and is part of the GGPO-saved block, so it belongs in the preset, not in the renderer.';

UPSERT finding:setting9_config_0x2b0_attack_multiplier_keep SET status='inferred', confidence='medium', date='2026-09-06',
  title='config+0x2b0 (MvC2 setting 9, strid 0xa62, default 0, online 1) gates one line: the per-character reset method 0x140707660 zeroes the attacker damage multiplier entity+0x2b5 only when config+0x2b0 == 0',
  statement='0x140707660 (no Ghidra function; capstone): mov rax,[0x140acd3a0]; cmp dword [rax+0x2b0],0; jne skip; mov byte [rcx+0x2b5],0; skip: memset(rcx+0x36c, 0, 0x100) -- referenced from the per-character method table slot 0x140a90298 and from 0x14070747f. entity+0x2b5 is read by the damage formula FUN_14063cd30 as an attacker-side multiplier: damage *= (+0x2b5 or +0x536) * DAT_14097eb40 (= 1/32) when non-zero; entity+0x2b6 (or +0x537) is the defender-side counterpart. Writers: FUN_14068ff30 (900-frame character buffs: case 1 -> +0x2b5 = 0x28 = x1.25, case 9 -> +0x2b5 = +0x2b6 = 0x28, case 2 -> +0x2b6 = 0x10 = x0.5, case 3 -> entity+0x2b0 = 1 for 600 frames), switchD_14070809b::caseD_0 0x1407080ca (+0x2b5 = 0x30 = x1.5), and character code at 0x1406682b0, 0x14066888e, 0x140668934, 0x1406696d8, 0x14066a09d, 0x14066c318, 0x14066c3d5, 0x14066c921, 0x14066c983, 0x140685f2e, 0x140707555, 0x1407075a9, 0x140719e40, 0x140722440, 0x140722f7e, 0x140723895, 0x140732744.',
  caveat='WHICH event invokes the table-slot method (round start, tag, assist call) and which character owns 0x140707660 are UNKNOWN; the option name is UNKNOWN (late string id 0xa62, MvC2 only; MvC1 has a sibling 0xa66 with 3 choices). The value for ranked (1 = keep the multiplier) is CONFIRMED from the table.',
  consequence='Setting 9 = 1 is part of the ranked preset. It changes damage in the buff-carry case only; the vs-01-based gates cannot see it. Confirming the name needs the localisation file or a live A/B with a character buff across the reset.';

UPSERT finding:supergun_ranked_preset_write_set SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-06',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='SUPERGUN RANKED preset: config+0x28c..0x2b0 = [2,1,1,2,2,0,1,7,1,1], config+0x7f4 = 2, written before FUN_140608690; if blk is restored after the carve also wr8(blk+0x3CE0, 1); mode words optional and each a change to the sim until gated',
  statement='A (values CONFIRMED = table 0x140a485a0 + i*0x24 + 0x10 via FUN_140050ec0): wr32(config+0x28c, 2) difficulty; wr32(config+0x290, 1) damage x1.0; wr32(config+0x294, 1) clock 120 frames/tick; wr32(config+0x298, 2) TURBO1 period 4; wr32(config+0x29c, 2) free play; wr32(config+0x2a0, 0); wr32(config+0x2a4, 1) flash off; wr32(config+0x2a8, 7) all secret characters; wr32(config+0x2ac, 1) colours = unlocks; wr32(config+0x2b0, 1) keep attack multiplier; leave config+0x2b4..0x2c8 = 0 and config+0x284/0x286/0x288 = 0xff; wr32(config+0x7f4, 2). WHEN: after the exe_image page restore and before any mode entry / re-carve (FUN_140607b50 -> FUN_140608690 bakes them). B (blk restored after the carve, FUN_140608690 will not re-run): wr8(blk+0x3CE0, 1) = G+0x28; every other G byte already equals the ranked value in vs-01/select-01/20260903 anchors (G+0x1b 1, G+0x46 1, G+0x49 2, G+0x4f 1, G+0x4d 2, G+0x2a 1 in versus, G+0xa6 0, masks 0xf8ffffff/0x07ffffff, blk+0x3c40/0x3c43 = 1). Keep the seed-189 speed write-set (G+0x89 = G+0x49 = 2). C (optional, only to make the state read as ranked; sim effects listed in finding:online_only_game_code_branches): wr32(config+0x7b4, 1), wr32(config+0x7b8, 1), wr32(config+0x7bc, 1), wr32(config+0x80c, 0); session 0xd0320 = 1, 0xd0328 = 1, 0xd0374 = 1, 0xd037c = 1, 0xd0338 = 0; hostdev+0x1cd = 1. Training-side fields (config+0x828, +0x850.., +0x878/0x87c regen, +0x880/0x884 meter) must be 0 as in vs-01.',
  consequence='Every write here is a change to the simulation until gated (rule 4). The fixed gate is the battle-entry blk against one a live RANKED match produced for the same roster and stage; no ranked anchor exists yet (UNKNOWN), and the vs-01 anchor cannot see the two differing settings (G+0x28 only shows at a KO strobe, config+0x2b0 only in a buff-carry). Next step: capture one ranked pre/ anchor (blk.bin, exe_image.bin, host_device.bin) and diff config+0x284..0x2c8, G+0x28, blk+0x6ce4.. against this preset.';

UPSERT finding:sh4_steam_pairs_ranked_settings SET status='inferred', confidence='high', date='2026-09-06',
  title='SH4<->Steam pairs for the settings block: GameGlobal+0x30 0x8C268270 Char Unlocks <-> G+0x30/0x34 (blk+0x3CE8/0x3CEC), GameGlobal+0x38 0x8c268278 Color Unlocks <-> G+0x38/0x3c (blk+0x3CF0/0x3CF4); G+0x28 0x8c268268 has no SH4 annotation (collection-era)',
  statement='refs/marvelous2/work.asm lines 20-21 annotate 0x8C268270 Char Unlocks and 0x8c268278 Color Unlocks; with G = blk+0x3CB8 <-> 0x8c268240 (seed 189: G+0x89 <-> 0x8c2682c9) these are G+0x30 and G+0x38, exactly the two mask pairs FUN_140608690 builds from config+0x2a8 (DAT_140a69de0 groups) and copies under config+0x2ac, and that FUN_140628df0 ORs into the select availability masks blk+0x33a18/0x33a1c (base 0xc0fcfaff | 0x1803300) and blk+0x33a44/0x33a48 per side. Fingerprints: the 7x4 character-id group table DAT_140a69de0, the 0xc0fcfaff base mask, the 1/32 damage scale DAT_14097eb40 with the 0x10/0x20/0x30/0x40 table, the 180/120/90/70 clock table -- never instruction bytes. 0x8c268268 (G+0x28) does not appear in refs/marvelous2, and FUN_14060b440 (boot defaults, the DC init_default_settings twin) does not write it: the screen-flash byte is a Steam addition inside GameGlobal.',
  consequence='The unlock/colour masks are game settings on Steam (menu-driven), not save-file progress as on DC; a runner must carry them in config (0x2a8 = 7, 0x2ac = 1) or the select screen loses the 28 secret characters and their colours.';

